unit("Vasopressin Antagonists and Management of SIADH",
     "Vasopressin antagonists are used in SIADH: conivaptan is given intravenously in emergencies, and for maintenance/long-term oral therapy tolvaptan (limited to one month because of hepatotoxicity) or mozavaptan are used. SIADH is managed acutely by severity: mild cases get free water restriction with sodium tablets, while moderate cases (lethargy, confusion) and severe cases (seizures) get hypertonic saline. Long-term maintenance is free water restriction with or without sodium tablets.")
q(112, 'In emergencies of SIADH, the vasopressin antagonist given is:', ['Conivaptan (I/v)', 'Tolvaptan', 'Mozavaptan', 'Desmopressin'], 'The emergencies line says conivaptan (I/v).')
q(112, 'For maintenance/long-term therapy of SIADH, the oral vasopressin antagonists are tolvaptan and:', ['Mozavaptan', 'Conivaptan', 'Desmopressin', 'Terlipressin'], 'The oral bracket covers tolvaptan and mozavaptan.')
q(112, 'Tolvaptan is limited to one month of use due to:', ['Hepatotoxicity', 'Nephrotoxicity', 'Ototoxicity', 'Cardiotoxicity'], 'The tolvaptan line says up to one month due to hepatotoxicity.')
q(112, 'In mild acute SIADH, the treatment is free water restriction plus:', ['Sodium tablets', 'Hypertonic saline', 'Vasopressin', 'Furosemide'], 'The mild branch says free water restriction + sodium tablets.')
q(112, 'Moderate acute SIADH presents with:', ['Lethargy and confusion', 'Seizures only', 'No symptoms', 'Coma only'], 'The moderate branch lists lethargy and confusion.')
q(112, 'Severe acute SIADH presents with:', ['Seizures', 'Lethargy only', 'Confusion only', 'Headache only'], 'The severe branch lists seizures.')
q(112, 'Both moderate and severe acute SIADH are treated with:', ['Hypertonic saline', 'Free water restriction alone', 'Vasopressin', 'Desmopressin'], 'The bracket over moderate and severe points to hypertonic saline.')
q(112, 'Long-term maintenance in SIADH consists of free water restriction with or without:', ['Sodium tablets', 'Hypertonic saline', 'Vasopressin antagonist', 'Loop diuretic'], 'The long-term branch says free water restriction +/- sodium tablets.')

unit("Diuretics: Summary Table",
     "The summary table places each diuretic class with its target: carbonic anhydrase inhibitors act on PCT carbonic anhydrase (acetazolamide, used in acute mountain sickness, causing renal stones, hypokalemia, metabolic acidosis, sulfonamide hypersensitivity and hyperammonemia that contraindicates them in liver cirrhosis), loop diuretics block Na+/K+/2Cl- in the thick ascending loop (furosemide, DOC in pulmonary edema, and if GFR is below 40 loops remain DOC with metolazone added if there is no response), thiazides block Na+/Cl- in the DCT (chlorthalidone, first-line in HTN, increasing Ca2+ so they are used in HTN with osteoporosis), potassium-sparing diuretics act on aldosterone receptors or ENaC (spironolactone DOC in cirrhotic edema causing gynecomastia; amiloride DOC in lithium-induced DI) and mannitol acts on loop more than PCT (DOC in cerebral edema, acute congestive glaucoma and diuretic disequilibrium).")
q(112, 'The target of carbonic anhydrase inhibitors in the summary table is:', ['PCT: carbonic anhydrase', 'TAL: Na+/K+/2Cl-', 'DCT: Na+/Cl-', 'Collecting duct: ENaC'], 'The CA inhibitor row gives PCT: carbonic anhydrase.')
q(112, 'The CA inhibitor drug named in the summary table is:', ['Acetazolamide', 'Dichlorphenamide', 'Methazolamide', 'Brinzolamide'], 'The CA inhibitor row names acetazolamide.')
q(112, 'The use given for acetazolamide in the summary table is:', ['Acute mountain sickness', 'Pulmonary edema', 'Cirrhotic edema', 'Diuretic disequilibrium'], 'The acetazolamide row says acute mountain sickness.')
q(112, 'The summary table lists renal stones, hypokalemia and metabolic acidosis as side effects of:', ['CA inhibitors', 'Loop diuretics', 'Thiazides', 'Mannitol'], 'The CA inhibitor row lists these side effects.')
q(112, 'Hypersensitivity with rash and bone marrow suppression is listed for:', ['CA inhibitors', 'Loop diuretics', 'K+ sparing diuretics', 'Mannitol'], 'The CA inhibitor row lists hypersensitivity including rash and BM suppression.')
q(112, 'The CA inhibitor row lists increased NH4+ with the contraindication of:', ['Liver cirrhosis', 'Renal failure', 'COPD', 'Pregnancy'], 'The CA inhibitor row says up NH4+: C/I liver cirrhosis.')
q(112, 'The summary table lists amiloride as the "diuretic" for which class?', ['CA inhibitors', 'Loop diuretics', 'Thiazides', 'K+ sparing diuretics'], 'The amiloride mention sits in the CA inhibitor row listing a diuretic.')
q(112, 'The target of loop diuretics in the summary table is:', ['Thick ascending loop: Na+/K+/2Cl-', 'PCT: carbonic anhydrase', 'DCT: Na+/Cl-', 'Loop > PCT'], 'The loop row gives thick ascending loop: Na+/K+/2Cl-.')
q(112, 'In the summary table, the DOC use of furosemide is:', ['Pulmonary edema', 'Cerebral edema', 'Acute mountain sickness', 'Cirrhotic edema'], 'The loop row says DOC: pulmonary edema.')
q(112, 'According to the loop row, if GFR is below 40 the DOC remains:', ['Loop diuretics', 'Thiazides', 'CA inhibitors', 'K+ sparing diuretics'], 'The loop row says if GFR <40, DOC: loop diuretics.')
q(112, 'Metolazone is added in the loop row when there is:', ['No response', 'Hyperkalemia', 'Hypertension', 'Hypercalcemia'], 'The loop row says metolazone added if no response.')
q(112, 'The loop diuretic row lists decreased Ca2+ with the use of treating:', ['Hypercalcemia', 'Hypocalcemia', 'Osteoporosis', 'Renal stones'], 'The loop row says down Ca2+: Rx hypercalcemia.')
q(112, 'Hyperglycemia and hyperuricemia are side effects listed for loop diuretics and:', ['Thiazides', 'CA inhibitors', 'Mannitol', 'K+ sparing diuretics'], 'The table lists these effects for loop diuretics with thiazides having similar effects.')
q(112, 'The target of thiazides in the summary table is:', ['DCT: Na+/Cl-', 'TAL: Na+/K+/2Cl-', 'PCT: carbonic anhydrase', 'ENaC'], 'The thiazide row gives DCT: Na+/Cl-.')
q(112, 'The thiazide drug named in the summary row is:', ['Chlorthalidone', 'Metolazone', 'Indapamide', 'Chlorothiazide'], 'The thiazide row names chlorthalidone.')
q(112, 'The use of thiazides in the summary table is:', ['1st line drug in HTN', 'DOC pulmonary edema', 'DOC cerebral edema', 'Acute mountain sickness'], 'The thiazide row says 1st line drug in HTN.')
q(112, 'Increased Ca2+ in the thiazide row supports use in HTN with:', ['Osteoporosis', 'Gout', 'Hypercalcemia', 'Renal stones'], 'The thiazide row says up Ca2+: Rx HTN with osteoporosis.')
q(112, 'The two targets named for K+ sparing diuretics are aldosterone receptor blockers and:', ['ENaC blockers', 'Na+/Cl- cotransporter', 'Na+/K+/2Cl-', 'Aquaporins'], 'The K+ sparing row lists aldosterone receptor blockers and ENaC blockers.')
q(112, 'In the summary table, spironolactone is DOC for:', ['Cirrhotic edema', 'Pulmonary edema', 'Acute glaucoma', 'Diuretic disequilibrium'], 'The spironolactone row says DOC: cirrhotic edema.')
q(112, 'The side effect listed with spironolactone in the summary table is:', ['Gynecomastia', 'Erectile dysfunction', 'Ototoxicity', 'Renal stones'], 'The K+ sparing row lists gynecomastia.')
q(112, 'In the summary table, amiloride is DOC for:', ['Li induced DI', 'Cirrhotic edema', 'Pulmonary edema', 'Cerebral edema'], 'The amiloride row says DOC: Li induced D.I.')
